# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without this file a Windows
# clone checks out bin/*.sh with CRLF line endings — and every helper then dies
# at `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` with "bad interpreter", before any other Windows
# problem is even reachable. Pin the shebang'd scripts to LF unconditionally so
# clone behavior can't depend on the cloning machine's autocrlf setting.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
